LAST_SUCCESS=Diagnosed desktop UI-oversized-until-maximize (WSLg): the GL present path (default) lacks the live-size reconcile the softbuffer path has, AND a WANDR_DESKTOP_SIZE taller/wider than the monitor produces a compositor-clamped window while winit keeps reporting the UNCLAMPED requested size (verified: 1440x2880 requested, screen 3840x2160, inner_size stays 1440x2880, no Resized) -> guest lays out too big until a manual maximize fires a real Resized. Fixes: (1) clamp WANDR_DESKTOP_SIZE to the monitor work area preserving aspect (1440x2880 -> 1032x2064, verified fires); (2) per-frame inner_size reconcile in RedrawRequested (resize + dispatch_resize_routed) for GL/async-size robustness.
NOTES=Task 115 COMPLETE + audio.player migrated. This is a NEW desktop bug (call it task 117). Visual fix NOT yet user-confirmed (couldn't screenshot the WSLg window). If not fixed, need user's exact command (WANDR_DESKTOP_SIZE value?), which app, and screen resolution. Diagnostic [geom] logs kept (clamp/Resized/reconcile — low noise). Rebuilt desktop p3-async host.
